    sha256: fc4496aae0bb510fea99ee047b82bbb00182dd336af8dfb065ef040f3967078f
  body: "# Own occupation and personal capability tests in the legacy guidance\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\
    \nThe captured incapacity chapter requires the decision maker to identify which of its two tests applies:
    the own occupation test or the personal capability assessment.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe chapter’s
    listed uses include Incapacity Benefit, Severe Disablement Allowance and particular IS/JSA or credit
    contexts. DMG 13002 expressly excludes IIDB, SSP and ESA. These tests must not be relabelled as ESA
    or UC work capability assessments, or assumed to establish current benefit entitlement.\n\n## Inspected
    source passages\n\n- [DMG 13001, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a74dd8b40f0b65f61322dcd/dmgch13.pdf#page=6)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 13: Incapacity for work.\n- [DMG 13002, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a74dd8b40f0b65f61322dcd/dmgch13.pdf#page=6)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 13: Incapacity for work.\n- [DMG 13025, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a74dd8b40f0b65f61322dcd/dmgch13.pdf#page=6)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 13: Incapacity for work.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch13`: PDF SHA-256 `fc4496aae0bb510fea99ee047b82bbb00182dd336af8dfb065ef040f3967078f`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `1c3e2ae8cf5c3f45273274f24d1bafff88d21a657237c557d555fed53088c931`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/common-incapacity-alternative-evidence
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source separately identifies evidence supporting incapacity; the evidence route
      does not remove the need to select the applicable legacy test.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch13/0006
      quote: "13025   There are two tests of incapacity\n\n        1.       the OOT (see DMG 13200) and\n\
        \n        2.       the PCA (see DMG 13300).\n\n        The DM must first determine which test
        applies."
      locator: DMG 13025
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch13/0010
      quote: "13101   Evidence of incapacity should be provided for the day or days of incapacity for
        work\n        until the person has been assessed for the PCA. Evidence may be\n              \
        \                  1\n        1.    self-certification (see DMG 13120) or\n                  \
        \                         2\n        2.    a statement from a doctor (see DMG 13140) or\n\n  \
        \      3.     if it is unreasonable to require such a statement, other evidence which is\n   \
        \            sufficient to show that the person should refrain from work because of some\n   \
        \                                                                      3\n               specific
        disease or bodily or mental disablement (see DMG 13160).\n                                   \
        \       1 SS (Med Ev) Regs, reg 5; 2 reg 2(1); SS (IW) (Gen) Regs, reg 6(1)(a);\n            \
        \                                                                       3 SS (Med Ev) Regs, reg
        2(1A)"
      locator: DMG 13101
